    "created_at": "2018-10-13T09:25:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-10-13T09:25:56Z",
    "body": "The microformats wiki still includes the defunct captcha for user registration.\r\n\r\nAdditionally passing the captcha is required in order to post external links (references, links to implementations, examples …), but it has not been possible to pass it anymore for months. [This has been known to site administrators for at least four months](http://microformats.org/wiki/index.php?title=admin-to-do&diff=66828&oldid=66827).\r\n\r\nSorry, but this is unacceptable for a website which is officially responsible for HTML's ``rel`` extensions and thereby also determines whether HTML errors are reported by HTML validators or not. Please fix microformats.org as soon as possible or create an alternative solution to register ``rel`` values.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/429525549/reactions",
