    "created_at": "2019-08-08T15:02:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-08T15:02:09Z",
    "body": "I also don't think it makes any sense for the spec to direct users to a wiki to register new authorized values. Note that the spec also says that conformance checkers are expected to somehow scrape the wiki to find the correct values, and that they should also offer to add unknown values to the wiki.\r\n\r\nThis problem has been discussed already on the two previous bugtrackers, since 2011:\r\n* https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=17899\r\n* https://github.com/w3c/html/issues/160\r\n\r\nNow that registration on the wiki is dead, I really think it's time that the set of allowed values be moved to the spec. Barring this, the spec should clearly indicate that conformance checkers should accept any value and not pretend that the set of allowed values is normatively maintained on a defunct wiki.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
